

first create keystore with keytool

keytool -genkeypair \
  -alias keycloak \
  -keyalg RSA \
  -keystore keycloak.jks \
  -storepass password \
  -keypass password \
  -validity 3650 \
  -dname "CN=localhost, OU=Dev, O=MyCompany, L=City, ST=State, C=US"



  now check the keystore file location with below command
  ls /Users/deadlock/keycloak

  you should see the below things
  keycloak.jks

  if not , move it there
  mv ~/keycloak.jks /Users/deadlock/keycloak/

  Now check inside the docker
  docker run --rm -v /Users/deadlock/keycloak:/opt/keycloak/conf alpine ls /opt/keycloak/conf


  The below are keycloak with admin without db


  now start keycloak with https
  docker run -p 8443:8443 \
    -v /Users/deadlock/keycloak:/opt/keycloak/conf \
    -e KC_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_USERNAME=admin \
    -e KC_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=YourStrongPassword123 \
    quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.5.3 \
    start-dev \
    --https-key-store-file=/opt/keycloak/conf/keycloak.jks \
    --https-key-store-password=password \
    --hostname-strict=false
     --hostname=192.168.1.5




